---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { projects } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Javier Ponz — AI systems & full stack">
  <section class="hero"><p class="kicker">Aberdeen, Scotland</p><h1>I build agent tooling and small products that <span class="serif">actually ship</span>.</h1><p class="lede">Ten years diagnosing hard technical problems for people at Apple Retail, now building AI systems and full stack applications — deployed, tested, and running in production. Same job, different surface.</p></section>
  <section class="grid"><span class="label">01 / Overview</span><div class="copy"><h2>Technical operator turned builder.</h2><p>A decade at Apple Retail taught me to diagnose failure fast, work in ambiguity, and translate technical complexity into something a person can act on — first at the counter, later leading the teams doing it. I now apply that to AI systems: agent workflows, automation, and applications I take all the way to production on infrastructure I run myself.</p><p>I am studying Artificial Intelligence and Full Stack development at Universidad Rey Juan Carlos, and I ship real things while I do it — this site, a live web app, an MCP server, and agent skill packs. Everything here has source code you can read.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">leading is serving</span><span class="tag">agent workflows</span><span class="tag">Docker & deployment</span><span class="tag">technical troubleshooting</span><span class="tag">MCP</span><span class="tag">building in public</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="grid"><span class="label">02 / Explore</span><div class="cards"><a class="card" href="/about"><span class="meta">Background</span><h3>About & experience →</h3><p>Apple Retail, the move into AI systems, and the credentials behind it.</p></a><a class="card" href="/workbench"><span class="meta">Build log</span><h3>Workbench →</h3><p>Projects and repositories, with scope and status stated plainly.</p></a><a class="card" href="/memento-mori"><span class="meta">Case study</span><h3>Shipping to production →</h3><p>How a small app got from idea to a live, verified deployment.</p></a><a class="card" href="/thesis"><span class="meta">Thesis</span><h3>The malleable machine →</h3><p>Open agent primitives, an editable OS, and why they are converging.</p></a></div></section>
  <section class="grid"><span class="label">03 / Selected work</span><div class="rows">{projects.slice(0,3).map((project) => <a class="row" href={project.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><time>{project.kind}</time><div><h3>{project.title} ↗</h3><p>{project.description}</p></div></a>)}</div></section>
</Layout>
